WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.950
Yugi's Difficult Battle
Orgoth the Relentless's Fierce Attack

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.530
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.200
L-O-V-E Otogi!

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.200
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.200
Beat Yugi the cheater!

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.720
Be quiet!

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.460
What all of a sudden?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.900
A dog can't talk!

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.880
I'll say one thing!

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:47.600
I can't forgive you for saying that Yugi cheated in his wholehearted duel during Duelist Kingdom!

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.170
That's right.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.890
Pegasus was the one who used suspicious tricks, like Mind Scan!

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.770
Nothing you say will change Otogi's mind.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:04.710
He's convinced that Yugi stole his dream.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.880
Then what should we do?

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:09.730
There's only one option.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.910
Yugi must use this game to make Otogi understand how he feels.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.020
Yeah!

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.020
This battle isn't just for me anymore!

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.790
Yugi, this battle is to defend your honor!

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.760
Quit your yapping!

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.500
You...loser...dog!

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.140
You...loser...dog!

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:26.960
You...loser...dog!

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.960
A...loser...dog!

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.930
A...loser...dog!

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.880
A...loser...dog?

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.970
I'm a loser dog...

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.460
Jonouchi's spirit has been instantly crushed.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.860
The phrase "loser dog" has caused psychological damage.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.980
That's the howl of a loser dog.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.450
How can I make Otogi understand?

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.460
There must be a hint in this game.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.420
Dice roll!

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:08.700
Otogi created this game, so fully understanding it is the best way to reach his heart.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.710
These crests will let me use an effect.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:23.750
I use three Magic Crests to move Thunder Ball in a straight line.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.700
If it strikes a monster or item, it'll destroy it and stop moving.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.960
Is that correct?

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:29.680
Yeah.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.460
I use three Magic Crests.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.730
Rolling Crush!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.480
I'll use the effect again!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.710
I use three Magic Crests to do Rolling Crush again!

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.370
No!

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.590
Woof woof!

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.090
Good!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.060
Why is there a crowd?

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.420
Are they selling the new game that I heard about?

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.450
Excuse me.  Coming through.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.310
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.320
You can do it, Otogi!

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.200
This is too much stimulation for an old man!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.460
What?

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.530
Yugi?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.360
How dare you participate in a rival store's demo duel!

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.830
Keep it quiet, geezer!

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.480
This is the good part!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.620
You're in our way!

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.420
We can't see a thing!

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.840
I'm sorry.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.840
Monsters can only attack once per turn.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.980
But effects can be used consecutively.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.680
Yugi, I'm surprised you figured that out.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.090
And I thought you were just a coward.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.970
When we started this game, I was confused.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:18.600
But I'm starting to understand how fun Dungeon Dice Monsters is!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:25.140
I can see why you planned to release this game worldwide.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.500
Of course.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.140
Did you think those words would win me over?

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.650
A battle is a battle!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.880
Yeah.  The game is just beginning!

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.880
It's my turn!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.720
Dice roll!

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.390
My summon failed.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.390
It's my turn.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.390
Dice roll!

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.900
Yeah!  I can summon!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.420
Dimension Dice!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.230
I summon Knight of Twin Swords!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.440
None of my monsters can attack the opponent.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.790
I'll store the Movement Crest in my crest pool.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.520
You're getting the hang of this game, Yugi.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.530
What?  I don't get it.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:28.060
You still don't understand the rules of this game?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:34.000
After summoning a monster, you don't have to use your dice crests that turn.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.070
You can store them in your crest pool for future use.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:40.080
Now I get it!

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.890
You're so slow.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.750
And you thought you could challenge Otogi?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.210
That's why you ended up as a loser dog.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.100
This isn't good.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.090
He's done for.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:03.640
Yugi is learning this game quickly by reading the manual on his monitor.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:09.480
But the more you comprehend this game, the more satisfying it will be to crush you.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.270
It's my turn!

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.110
Dice roll!

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.800
The Summon Crests match!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.280
Dimension Dice!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.430
I summon Level 2 Battle Ox!

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:34.020
I use my Movement Crests to move Battle Ox four squares forward.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.040
Battle Ox, attack Knight of Twin Swords!

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:54.460
Beasts are strong against Warriors, so it gains 10 attack points to 30!

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.090
I switch Knight of Twin Swords to defense position!

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.170
It has 10 defense points!

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:15.930
Knight of Twin Swords has 10 defense points, so it takes 20 points of damage.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.910
Its hit points drop to 10.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.910
He's mastered defending!

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.300
It's my turn!

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.410
Dice roll!

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:31.650
I use two Attack Crests to pay for a special attack.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.930
Twin Sword Continuous Slash!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.180
My Battle Ox...

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.180
Otogi!

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:01.850
It's his first time playing this game, but Yugi is doing great!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.690
Yugi, keep it up!

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:09.510
Otogi, I feel like I'm finally standing on the same starting line as you.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:20.770
Destroying Battle Ox was impressive.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:27.340
But if you think that means you truly understand Dungeon Dice Monsters, you're very wrong.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:28.580
What?

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:33.260
Monster battles aren't the only determining factor in this game.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.580
What are you trying to say?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.590
You still don't know.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.420
Look closely at the field.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.380
Oh no!

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:25.700
Oh no!

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.770
What's going on?

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.910
Did Yugi overlook something?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:35.350
Allow me to explain.

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:44.760
When you place a die on the field to summon a monster, it must connect to your own dungeon.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:56.130
Otogi's previous dice dimension blocked the path of Yugi's dungeon.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.870
Which means Yugi...

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:00.880
Correct.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.370
Yugi can no longer stretch his territory towards me.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.880
Isn't there any other way?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:12.880
Well, monsters can move through the opponent's dungeon.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.120
The opponent's dungeon?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:23.630
But you can't get near me - the Dungeon Master - without defeating many monsters.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:24.970
No way!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:27.420
That's impossible, even for Yugi!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.400
It's my turn.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.430
Here it is!

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:39.010
Yugi, look at this die.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.010
A black die?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.840
It's known as a "Rare Black."

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.800
Watch what happens when I dimension a black die.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.150
Dice roll!

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:57.490
I can summon!

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.990
Dimension Rare Black!

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:15.780
I summon Level 3 Warp Vortex.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.500
What's that?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.560
It's a warp item.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:22.280
Warp?

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:27.290
Rare Blacks contain special items, and this is one of them.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:33.820
But this item's effect only works when there are two Rare Blacks on the field.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.650
One is the entrance, and the other is the exit.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:39.300
You can instantly warp between the two.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:41.940
I see!

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:50.040
He left an area open in my territory so that he can dimension Warp Vortex's exit in my territory!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.470
You've finally caught on.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:13:01.120
My goal is to place another Rare Black in your territory so that I can send my army of monsters instantly.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:06.530
When I complete this Rare Black combo, victory is mine.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.080
Warp Vortex...

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.530
I'll strengthen my defenses for now.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:13.800
Dice roll!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:16.300
I'm allowed to summon!

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:17.600
All right!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.380
Dimension Dice!

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:30.220
I summon Level 3 Strike Ninja!

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.680
Strike Ninja has arrived!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.110
Strike Ninja is a nice monster.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:41.830
But can its speed beat my Rare Black combo?

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.350
My black die has arrived.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:54.210
If I dimension this, my Rare Black combo will be complete!

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.440
Oh no!

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.210
Go, Otogi!

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.380
Dice roll!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.650
This is bad.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.720
If he completes his Rare Black combo...

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.330
You get to survive.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.360
What's this?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.210
Otogi, you overlooked one thing.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.710
I also have a Rare Black!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.210
Say what?

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.520
Yugi!

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.920
Dice roll!

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.950
I can summon!

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:45.460
Dimension Rare Black Dice!

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:56.400
Strike Ninja uses its movement effect!

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:09.570
What?

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:21.590
Strike Ninja attacks Ryu-Kishin!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.600
Your life is mine!

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:34.240
Good!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.640
He did it!

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:36.190
All right!

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.110
Another one is destroyed!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:45.800
By spreading his dungeon over the entire field, Otogi stopped my own dungeon.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:51.370
The only way I can win is to invade his territory by using this Warp Vortex.

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:58.050
He used Warp Vortex before I could place my Warp Crest.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.910
Strike Ninja is a fast and agile monster.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.970
It can move three spaces with one Movement Crest.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:09.910
Yugi can definitely attack me next turn.

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:14.110
I must summon a monster to defend me this turn!

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.290
My summon failed!

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.990
Dice roll!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:24.530
All right!  I rolled Movement Crests!

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.040
Run, Strike Ninja!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:36.640
Strike Ninja, attack Otogi the Dungeon Master!

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.570
Your life is mine!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:51.220
Oh no!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.220
How horrible!

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:54.640
He did it!

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.090
Now they're even!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:57.300
All right!

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.900
Well done!

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.750
That's why you're my grandson!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:01.670
You're in the way!

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:02.950
Move, geezer!

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:15.280
You managed to damage the inventor of Dungeon Dice Monsters.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.880
No wonder you're Duelist Kingdom champion.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:20.750
You're making me excited, Yugi.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:26.220
But I won't let you lay a finger on me anymore!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.890
Good!  My Summon Crests match!

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:33.910
Here I go!

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.390
Dimension Dice!

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:48.770
I summon Level 3 Orgoth the Relentless.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:55.910
Orgoth the Relentless's effect uses two Magic Crests to raise its attack points from 20 to 30.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:18:00.020
Then I use Movement Crests to move Orgoth the Relentless.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.530
Orgoth the Relentless, attack Strike Ninja!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.180
Diamond Blade!

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:15.530
At this rate, it'll be destroyed!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.120
It's destroyed.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.340
Are you sure?

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.080
What?

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.310
Look closely at your dungeon.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.200
Pitiful.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:40.220
No way!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:46.250
When Orgoth the Relentless attacked, I used a Trap Crest to activate its effect.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:50.940
Strike Ninja can dodge attacks and effects.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:54.310
You've recovered from the brink of defeat.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.050
Your quick judgments are amazing.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.170
I can't believe this is the first time you're playing DDM.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:08.450
Maybe Yugi Muto could've defeated Pegasus without cheating.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:10.960
It's my turn!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.110
Strike Ninja attacks!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:19.800
What?

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:21.910
He did it!

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.810
One more attack, and I win.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.570
Yugi, I won't let things go your way.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:34.310
This battle is to get my dream back!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.170
It's my turn!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.870
Orgoth the Relentless attacks Strike Ninja!

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:48.450
I don't have any Trap Crests in my crest pool.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.430
There's no way I can avoid this attack.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.670
Diamond Blade!

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:55.770
I'm done for!

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:07.290
The only monster I got into enemy territory is now destroyed.

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:12.020
My opponent has three monsters and one unknown item.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:14.650
I only have three monsters.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:17.920
What should I do?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:36.470
Orgoth the Relentless uses Warp Vortex to enter Yugi's dungeon and destroy all his monsters.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:40.620
If he doesn't summon a monster soon, he'll run out of life points!

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:43.820
But he doesn't have the space to summon a monster!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.350
Don't lose, Yugi!

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.650
There must be something you can do!

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:51.900
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Miracle Dimension
Summon Dark Magician

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.620
Duel, standby!

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:07.750
The flask glistens

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:15.600
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:24.570
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:32.350
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:38.180
Shower of happiness

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:42.290
I will shower you with it

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:50.560
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:54.800
Shower of happiness

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:58.930
You are not alone

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:05.650
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
